% c128: 101-104 trumpets and trombones crescendo pp -> f (were -> ff), the level they keep in the tutti from 105, so the brass do not drop a level on the arrival
%   (Adler II PDF 38-40: the arrival is the larger event); horns, strings, woodwinds and timpani ff at 104 unchanged. The repeated f at 105 removed (sC.ily).
% SCHERZO, development, bars 57-104.
% c035: 69 Fl 1/Ob 1 and the Bn 1 solo at 73 print "1." (the combiner reprints no label after a shared rest; Adler II PDF 312: "1." / "a2"); 71 Bn 1 crescendo from the downbeat with Bn 2, so the shared staff prints one hairpin.
% c022: 68 viola G sharp (was B): the 5th of iv7 falls to the leading tone; removes fifths D-A/E-B with the basses (A-S PDF 189-190, Ex. 12-20, 12-21).
% 57-72: fugato on the head of theme A: Vc and Bn 1 in G minor (57), violas in D minor over the cellos' countersubject (61),
%   Vln II in A minor over the violas' countersubject (65), stretto in all strings 69-72 onto A major, ff (V of D minor).
% 73-88: F major, the Neapolitan of E (A major -> F major is a falling major third, the symphony's key relation). No strings:
%   the harp has the theme head as a melody 73-80 (still unused colour: a melodic harp line); Cl 1 dolce 81-88, from D minor to the
%   Neapolitan sixth over A (85-86, chromatic tail C-B-B flat) and vii7 of E over A (87-88).
% c072: 88 A-sharp dim7 (bass A -> A sharp: the dim7 on natural 4 led on by the dim7 on sharp 4, A-S PDF 561, Ex. 31-14/31-15).
% 89-104: retransition over the B pedal (pizzicato basses, timpani motive x), the head rising Vla -> Vln II -> Vln I; hemiola build 101-104.

% c028: 72 the ff A-major chord decays (ff>) in winds and strings, as the horns already did, and the basses play it short: Adler II PDF 189-190
%   (an sf scored as a short note in one group against long decaying notes in others, Ex. XV-35 sf>pp), so F major enters pp at 73 without a dead cut.
% c042: 79 vii°7 of F (E-G-B flat-D flat: Hn 3 D-D flat-C, Bsn 1 A-B flat-A, harp LH E-G-B flat) replaces C7/E, the movement's only C-E-G sonority
%   (A-S PDF 374: V6/5 becomes vii°7 by replacing 5 with 6; PDF 393: vii°7 in major through flat 6; PDF 388, 395: flat 6 falls to 5).
% c042: 72-73 Hn 1 C sharp -> C natural and 85-87 Hn 4 F -> F sharp: each chromatic step in one voice, not split between voices (A-S PDF 394, Ex. 23-12).
% c028: 101-104 strings and woodwinds crescendo f -> ff with the brass and timpani (they were f flat, then ff on 104).
% c044: 72 the ff A-major chord had no E between the top E6 and the bass and nothing between A3 and A4: Vln II E5-C sharp 6, violas E4-A4, cellos A2-E3
%   as double stops (Adler II PDF 161, Schumann 1/i: non divisi double and triple stops for a ringing tutti chord; PDF 164, Brahms 3/i: every chord in every octave). Also 300.
% c097: 69-72 a real stretto at one-bar distance (Adler II PDF 44, 47: Bartok, Concerto for Orchestra i, mm. 363-386, entries one bar apart in
%   different groups; PDF 42-43: Hindemith's brass fugato, each entry in its best register): Vln I/Fl 1/Ob 1 on A at 69, Vln II/Cl 1 on E at 70
%   (they rested at 69; they had doubled Vln I a fourth/third below), Vc/Bsn 1 on A at 71 with Hn 1-2 in unison (Adler PDF 44: two horns in unison
%   equal one trumpet or trombone), over the A pedal. Vc/Bsn 1 hold E at 70 so their entry at 71 is fresh. Same at 297-300.
sBFluteOne = { R2.*12 | a''4-.\f^\markup \bold "1." e''8-. e''-. a''4-. | c'''2->( b''8 bes''8 | a''4-.) b''-.\< cis'''-. | e'''2.->\ff\> | R2.\! | R2.*15 | R2.*12 | b''2\f\< a''4~ | a''4 fis''2 | dis'''2 b''4~ | b''4 a''2-\tweak stencil ##f \ff | }
sBFluteTwo = { R2.*15 | a''2.->\ff\> | R2.\! | R2.*27 | fis''2.\f\< | fis''2. | fis''2. | fis''2.\ff | }
% c077: 92-94 the retransition's second head entry goes to Ob 1 (Vln II rests): the entries now pass viola -> oboe -> violins, as Beethoven 9/ii's ritmo di tre battute
%   (bars 177-195) passes its head between bassoons, oboes, clarinets and flutes over string punctuation (Adler PDF 253-255: gestures thrown between winds and strings,
%   the third time altered; PDF 271: imitation between winds and strings). The reprise retransition 241-252 keeps its all-string entries.
